[size=5][b]Cook a meal out of meals.[/b][/size]

Vanilla cooking stops at the stew. You make the Meat Stew, you eat the Meat Stew, you go back to the pot. Kitsune Kitchen asks the obvious next question: what if you put the stew, a baked potato and a boiled egg in the pot [i]together[/i]?

You get Hunter's Bounty. It's worth more than all three put together, and it comes with a buff.

22 new foods and drinks, all craftable from day one, none of them smelly to zombies. Plus one that's smelly on purpose.

[line]

[size=4][b]New in 1.5.0: the Harvest Menu[/b][/size]
Chickens and pumpkins showed up in vanilla and the fox noticed.
[list]
[*][b]Pumpkin Spice Latte.[/b] Coffee, pumpkin, honey. The world ended but the seasonal menu didn't. Gives you [b]Cozy[/b]: stamina regen and cold resistance for 20 minutes.
[*][b]Kitsune Udon.[/b] Miso, corn noodles, egg, and a golden fried pocket (animal fat, don't ask). In Japanese folklore kitsune udon is the fox's favorite food, so of course it's here. Gives you [b]Fox's Favor[/b]: better loot and faster looting for 20 minutes.
[*][b]Hot Honey Chicken.[/b] Your coop works hard. Nuggets, corn bread, hot honey.
[*][b]Harvest Pot Pie.[/b] Ash Chicken Stew under a pumpkin bread crust.
[*][b]Harvest Pumpkin Soup.[/b] The cheap early-game way to use those pumpkins.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Also in 1.5.0: the meals are worth it again[/b][/size]
Vanilla food got a big rebalance a while back and nobody told the fox. Most of the meals-made-of-meals ended up giving you [i]less[/i] than the dishes you fed into them. Kitsune Gumbo was eating 168 food worth of gumbo, tacos and corn and handing back 65. That's not a recipe, that's a tax.

Fixed. Every Completed Work now beats its ingredients eaten one by one, and then adds its buff on top. The two biggest, Kitsune Gumbo and Survivor's Feast, make [b]two servings[/b] per craft now. Their ingredients add up to more than a full stomach anyway, so the second bowl is for later. Or for your friend.

And a confession. The zero-smell food from 1.3.0 never actually worked. The game only reads smell from an item's eating action, and I'd put it on the item itself, so every dish quietly kept its vanilla smell. It works for real now. Sorry, zombies.

[line]

[size=4][b]Simple dishes[/b][/size]
Raw ingredients, campfire, done. Good for the first few days.
[list]
[*][b]Fox's Hash[/b] (grill): potato + egg
[*][b]Mushroom Omelette[/b] (grill): 2 mushrooms + egg
[*][b]Honey Corn Cake[/b] (grill): corn + honey. Keeps honey's little infection cure.
[*][b]Burnt Ends[/b] (grill): 2 charred meat + 4 raw meat. Your burnt meat finally has a purpose. Recipe by Maltaine.
[*][b]Forager's Broth[/b] (pot): 2 mushrooms + corn + boiled water
[*][b]Harvest Pumpkin Soup[/b] (pot): 2 pumpkins + corn + boiled water
[*][b]Kitsune Udon[/b] (pot): canned miso + 2 corn meal + egg + animal fat + boiled water. Fox's Favor.
[*][b]Country Fried Steak[/b] (pot): sham sandwich + 2 eggs + 2 grilled meat. Yes, the sham sandwich. Hearty. Also Maltaine's.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Drinks[/b][/size]
Smoothies are made in your backpack, like the Yucca Smoothie. Everything else is the cooking pot. Every drink puts you out if you're on fire.
[list]
[*][b]Blueberry Smoothie:[/b] 3 blueberries + boiled water
[*][b]Aloe Cooler:[/b] 2 aloe + blueberries + boiled water. Refreshed.
[*][b]Espresso Smoothie:[/b] coffee + a snowball. Wired: +15% run speed. Gotta go fast.
[*][b]Herbal Honey Tea:[/b] honey + aloe + yucca fibers + boiled water. Cures 15% infection (more than Herbal Antibiotics) and 20% dysentery. It replaces the vanilla Honey Tea recipe because it's just better. Vanilla Honey Tea still turns up in loot.
[*][b]Pumpkin Spice Latte:[/b] coffee + pumpkin + honey. Cozy.
[/list]

[size=4][b]Completed Works[/b][/size]
Meals made out of meals, in the cooking pot. Each is worth more than what went in, plus a buff.
[list]
[*][b]Fox's Breakfast:[/b] Bacon & Eggs + Corn Bread
[*][b]Wasteland Chowder:[/b] Sham Chowder + Corn on the Cob. Keeps the Sham Chowder Fortitude buff.
[*][b]Hot Honey Chicken:[/b] Chicken Nuggets + Corn Bread + Honey. Hearty.
[*][b]Hunter's Bounty:[/b] Meat Stew + Baked Potato + Boiled Egg. Hearty.
[*][b]Scavenger's Stir Fry:[/b] Vegetable Stew + Grilled Meat + Corn Bread. Energized.
[*][b]Harvest Pot Pie:[/b] Ash Chicken Stew + Pumpkin Bread. Hearty.
[*][b]Kitsune Gumbo[/b] (makes 2): Gumbo Stew + Fish Tacos + Corn on the Cob. Spicy, 30 minutes of damage resistance.
[*][b]Survivor's Feast[/b] (makes 2): Steak & Potato + Spaghetti + Blueberry Pie. Well Fed, 45 minutes of everything.
[/list]

[size=4][b]The cursed secret menu[/b][/size]
[b]Walker Milkshake.[/b] Rotting flesh, a blood bag, river water, blended at the workbench. Drink it and your smell maxes out for 60 seconds. Every walker within 100m comes to find out who smells so delicious.

It's horde bait. Drink it next to your trap line. Or don't, and find out the hard way why it's on the secret menu.

[size=4][b]The buffs[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Refreshed[/b] (5 min): light health + stamina regen
[*][b]Wired[/b] (10 min): +15% run speed, stamina regen
[*][b]Herbal Remedy[/b] (5 min): health regen
[*][b]Cozy[/b] (20 min): stamina regen, cold resistance
[*][b]Fox's Favor[/b] (20 min): +10% loot stage, 15% faster looting
[*][b]Hearty[/b] (15 min): health regen, +10% physical damage resistance
[*][b]Energized[/b] (15 min): stamina regen, +10% run speed
[*][b]Spicy[/b] (30 min): stamina regen, +15% physical damage resistance
[*][b]Well Fed[/b] (45 min): health + stamina regen, +15% damage resistance, +10% block damage
[/list]

[size=4][b]Plays nice with vanilla[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]A better Cooking Grill or Cooking Pot cooks Kitsune food faster, same as vanilla food. Pack Mule speeds up the smoothies.
[*]The Farmer armor set's food bonus works on Kitsune dishes.
[*]No magazines, no skill gates. Everything is unlocked from the start, which also means it works with progression overhauls like Learn By Doing that rip out the vanilla cooking skill.
[*]Bonus fix: traders will finally buy your Sham Sandwiches.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Unzip so you have [b]Mods/KitsuneKitchen/[/b] in your game folder (or %APPDATA%/7DaysToDie/Mods/).
[*]Restart the game.
[/list]
[list]
[*]7 Days to Die [b]V3.0 through V3.3[/b]
[*]XML only, no code. Works in single player and on dedicated servers.
[*]EAC off, like any modlet.
[*]Safe to add to an existing save.
[/list]

